      "id": "61f6f61cce52-q4",
      "number": 4,
      "question": "Statement: One aspirant was killed due to stampede while participating in a recruitment drive of police constables. Course of Action: I. The officials in charge of the recruitment process should immediately be suspended. II. A team of officials should be asked to find out the circumstances which led to the death of the aspirant and submit its report within a week. III. The Government should ask the home department to stagger the number of aspirants over more number of days to avoid such incidents in future.",
      "questionHtml": "<p>Statement: One aspirant was killed due to stampede while participating in a recruitment drive of police constables.</p><p>Course of Action:</p><p>I. The officials in charge of the recruitment process should immediately be suspended. </p><p>II. A team of officials should be asked to find out the circumstances which led to the death of the aspirant and submit its report within a week.</p><p>III. The Government should ask the home department to stagger the number of aspirants over more number of days to avoid such incidents in future.</p>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p>I. \"The officials in charge of the recruitment process should immediately be suspended.\" This course of action suggests taking immediate punitive action by suspending the officials in charge of the recruitment process. While it's essential to investigate and hold responsible parties accountable for such incidents, immediately suspending officials without a thorough inquiry might not be fair. Therefore, this action is not the best initial response.</p><p>II. \"A team of officials should be asked to find out the circumstances which led to the death of the aspirant and submit its report within a week.\" This course of action suggests a rational and responsible approach. It is crucial to investigate and understand the circumstances that led to the tragic event. A report within a week ensures a timely response to the incident. Investigating the matter thoroughly is a logical step.</p><p>III. \"The Government should ask the home department to stagger the number of aspirants over more number of days to avoid such incidents in the future.\" This course of action aims at preventing similar incidents in the future by spreading out the recruitment process over more days. This proactive measure can help manage crowds and reduce the chances of stampedes during recruitment drives. It focuses on prevention, which is a responsible approach.</p><p>Based on the above analysis: </p><p>Course of Action I may not be the best initial response as it suggests immediate suspension without a proper investigation.</p><p>Course of Action II is a logical and responsible step as it focuses on investigating the incident.</p><p>Course of Action III is also a reasonable measure to prevent future incidents.</p><p>So, the correct answer is (c) Only II and III follow.</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
